WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.420
Roughly 9.5 billion years ago, dark energy may have flipped from negative to positive, altering

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:12.140
how cosmic expansion is understood. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 253, an unseen

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.800
companion to a red giant, a young supernova in a barred spiral, and spectra of Uranus'

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:23.660
inner moons come next, then a cosmic spotlight. Scientists exploring an alternative gravity

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.920
theory, in a science daily account of the work, drew the finding from a branch of the theory

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:37.020
that had been overlooked, not from standard models. Red Giant J008 plus 0128 carries an

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:43.100
unseen binary companion. According to Fizz.org, found in Lammost and Apigee data,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:50.200
a red giant is a star in a late swollen phase. The companion's mass falls between 1.8 and 2.8

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:56.620
solar masses, with the best estimate sitting at 2.2 solar masses. The pair finishes a circuit in

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:00.060
about 3.3 years, and the path is nearly circular.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:06.440
Nothing in light shows up from the companion, which rules out an ordinary star, and 300,000

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:11.500
positon simulations of isolated binaries could not match the masses and orbital properties.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:17.280
The researchers conclude the companion is most likely a neutron star, the collapsed remnant

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.160
of a massive star, pushing the upper mass limit.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:29.128
Bard's spiral galaxy, NGC 14,333, 50 million light years away, gained a new feature from a young

00:01:29.128 --> 00:01:35.688
type 1A Supernova, a star's explosive demise. Images from the dark energy camera and Gemini

00:01:35.688 --> 00:01:42.568
South show Supernova SN 2026 Aavu, looking different from one night to the next, set against the

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:50.062
galaxy around it. The event was recorded toward Horologium in the Southern Sky. JWST Spectra of

00:01:50.062 --> 00:01:56.162
Uranus's innermost moons, as AAS Nova reports, open possible stories of how the ring moon

00:01:56.162 --> 00:01:57.102
system formed.

00:01:57.602 --> 00:02:01.982
The observations go after the moon's closest in, and a pass that looks messy.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:08.289
New research examined, in a study covered by universe today, a particularly dense galaxy

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:12.969
cluster for clues about why new stars have been forming more slowly since cosmic noon.

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:18.589
The study identifies mechanisms fostered by cluster density that strip away or heat the

00:02:18.589 --> 00:02:20.469
hydrogen that new stars require.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:25.010
Engineers at Colorado State University's Adaptive Robotics Lab

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.870
built a robot that changes shape, using

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.690
Tensegrity, an idea borrowed from architecture.

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:34.650
The design can cross broken boulders and slip into narrow cracks

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.450
that defeat wheels and rotors.

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.110
A recent paper in Nature Machine Intelligence

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:43.204
describes the morphology, applying gold nanoparticles

00:02:43.204 --> 00:02:45.244
in a planetary science journal paper

00:02:45.244 --> 00:02:51.484
by Nikita J. Borin and colleagues noted by A.A.S. Nova enhances the signal from molecules

00:02:51.484 --> 00:02:58.224
that matter for astrobiology, including histidine and vitamin K1, in mass spectrometry, which

00:02:58.224 --> 00:02:59.964
identifies molecules by mass.

00:03:00.684 --> 00:03:03.564
Silver nanoparticles did not work in those same tests.

00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:10.168
Mystery radio signals have been traced, in a case described by space.com, to an odd pairing,

00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:12.588
a white dwarf with a star like the sun.

00:03:12.588 --> 00:03:15.728
A white dwarf is the compact remnant of a star.

00:03:16.248 --> 00:03:20.968
The detection shows that radio wavelengths can show stellar storms more than 5,000 light

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:21.748
years from us.

00:03:22.799 --> 00:03:28.319
ESA's Euclid produced early results, according to Fizz.org, including an early image that

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:30.379
spans 60 square degrees of the sky.

00:03:30.939 --> 00:03:34.919
The release is a first step toward the full three-dimensional map the mission will make.

00:03:35.499 --> 00:03:40.679
Past observations already showed targets such as the Horsehead Nebula and the Perseus cluster.

00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:47.344
A researcher at Fry University, Berlin, extended, in work described by Universe Today, the

00:03:47.344 --> 00:03:51.804
old lunar tide model by folding in the cross polarization of gravitational waves.

00:03:52.324 --> 00:03:57.104
The work asks whether high precision tide records could show traces of space-time changing

00:03:57.104 --> 00:03:57.684
dynamically.

00:03:58.384 --> 00:04:03.364
Earth and the Moon make a tight test bed since those tides are already measured and well-described.

00:04:04.366 --> 00:04:10.026
In brief, Rocket Labs Electron lifted off from New Zealand in a flight noted by space.com,

00:04:10.026 --> 00:04:17.446
carrying an IQPS synthetic aperture radar satellite to 575 km altitude for the company's

00:04:17.446 --> 00:04:23.826
100th launch. NASA plans a Voyager 1 and 2 status update event for November 19th that

00:04:23.826 --> 00:04:28.806
will include mission updates, science from interstellar space, and a preview of an upcoming

00:04:28.806 --> 00:04:35.752
NASA Plus documentary. Gemini astronaut photos from 1966 helped argue for satellites devoted

00:04:35.752 --> 00:04:36.692
to watching Earth.

00:04:37.212 --> 00:04:42.392
Level and Aldrin shot the Red Sea and the Nile Valley on Gemini 12, showing that pictures

00:04:42.392 --> 00:04:44.772
from orbit are useful for studying the surface.

00:04:45.472 --> 00:04:50.032
Those frames fed William T. Pacora's campaign for the program that became Landsat.

00:04:50.652 --> 00:04:55.372
The photos showed that crops, floods, and how land is used could be tracked from orbit.

00:04:56.375 --> 00:05:02.015
Neutron stars form from the cores of exploded high mass stars and squeeze roughly 1.4 solar

00:05:02.015 --> 00:05:08.275
masses into a ball only about 20 kilometers across. Black holes by contrast usually start

00:05:08.275 --> 00:05:13.935
at 5 solar masses and go up. Between those two populations sits a thinly occupied band

00:05:13.935 --> 00:05:20.375
from roughly 2.5 to 5 solar masses, with few objects in it. That band is where the equations

00:05:20.375 --> 00:05:25.735
for matter under crushing pressure stop holding up a stable neutron star and allow a collapse

00:05:25.735 --> 00:05:31.615
into a black hole. No precise masses in hand for that transition, because the physics inside

00:05:31.615 --> 00:05:37.135
these objects is still poorly understood. A recent study published in Science Advances flagged a

00:05:37.135 --> 00:05:42.175
candidate that could help fix that limit. The open question is whether bodies in this range are

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:48.275
always neutron stars born unusually heavy, or whether some are the lightest black holes. One more

00:05:48.275 --> 00:05:53.575
detection that measures a radius, or that shows a solid surface, would decide it by showing whether

00:05:53.575 --> 00:05:59.235
the object can hold itself up against further collapse. Until then, every new fine trims the set

00:05:59.235 --> 00:06:02.515
of equations of state that ultra-dense matter is allowed to follow.

00:06:03.375 --> 00:06:08.835
November 19th is when NASA's Voyager 1 and 2 status event puts the latest interstellar

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:09.855
science on the table.

